{"type":"assistant","message":{"model":"claude-opus-5-5","id":"msg_011ChLtgNKZPJFPDEteN6cLi","type":"message","role":"assistant","content":[{"type":"text","text":"[x] lint, typecheck, and the TS test suite pass, and the Go build and Go tests still pass.\n\n`npx roast runs` and `npx roast runs show` now work, and all 13 acceptance criteria pass. The full `npm test` run passed (6320 of 6320) after the last code change, lint and typecheck are clean, and the Go build and `npm run test:go` pass. The tar failures from earlier attempts did not show up.\n\n**What changed:**\n- **`src/cli/runs.ts`** (new): the `runs` command with `--limit` and `--json`, and the `show <run-id>` subcommand. Run IDs are always resolved through the records module's `reportPath`, so `..`, `.` and `a/b` are rejected there (exit 4). Report output is escaped with `textBytes`, so invalid UTF-8 bytes also come out visibly escaped. Ticket 24 adds `checkout` and `prune` by appending to the exported `runsSubcommands`.\n- **`src/cli/commands.ts`**: registers `runs`. `run.ts` builds its command list from this file, so it needed no edit.\n- **`test/cli/runs.ts`** (new): 48 assertions that run the CLI in-process inside temporary Git repositories.\n- **`docs/agents/records.md`** and **`docs/agents/typescript.md`**: notes on the `runs` extension point and how to declare integer flags, since yargs number parsing is turned off.\n\n**How the criteria were checked:** the empty listing, outside-a-repo, `--json --limit` and formatted-output tests failed before the code that makes them pass. Most of the others passed as soon as they were written, because code from an earlier step or the shared parser already handled them. For each of those except the argument-count checks, I removed the relevant code (the `\\r` strip, the limit check, the escaping, run-ID validation, the missing-report error) and confirmed the test then fails. The positional-argument and argument-count rejections come from the shared parser.\n\n**One known gap:** the plain `runs` listing accepts a count written as `1.0` in an index line, while Go would reject that line and skip it. It only matters for hand-edited index files, and there is no test for it. It's recorded in `.redeye/notes.md`, which is not committed."}],"container":null,"stop_reason":null,"stop_sequence":null,"stop_details":null,"usage":{"input_tokens":2,"cache_creation_input_tokens":430,"cache_read_input_tokens":110001,"cache_creation":{"ephemeral_5m_input_tokens":0,"ephemeral_1h_input_tokens":430},"output_tokens":3,"service_tier":"standard","inference_geo":"global","speed":"standard"},"input_transformations":[],"diagnostics":null,"context_management":null},"parent_tool_use_id":null,"session_id":"1a6a4ea1-3c14-4268-8093-aa790c844327","uuid":"52ed632c-d270-4afc-bb63-6000fcc32ca1","timestamp":"2026-11-24T01:33:28.226Z","request_id":"req_011ChLtgNAPbjLN3pw24StbQ"}
